      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T15:31:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is one of those areas where there the documentation isn\u0027t clear and it is actually a lot easier to do than to find out how to do it. Making matters worse is that this workflow is different for different projects using git/gerrit (even chromium is different from chromiumos).\n\nThe procedure to follow is discussed here http://go/howdoicros/git_chromiumos_workflow#managing-multiple-dependent-cls \n but the gist of it is that if you have a series of git commits in your local branch then when you do a `repo upload` it is going to create a separate CL for each one and keep them chained together. \n \nLet me know if you want to chat about it and I can help you put together the chain.",
      "parentUuid": "3ef3c836_945fcb71",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 52
      },
